# Stray Vessel — scrub T2 basic striker (Color-saturated warrior, Tashkari blade)

[title Stray Vessel]
[image monsters/scrub_warrior_1.png]
[blood #6b3aa0]
[stats hp=18]

* move Attack
  narration: The Tashkari curve cuts at you in a remembered hand.
  narration: It shifts its weight and the blade comes around in a clean arc.

* move Defend
  narration: The Color across its skin slows. It turns its body sidelong.

* move Recover
  narration: The pulses settle. Whatever it lost, the Color is putting back.

* move Tainted Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: It plants its feet, the violet across its body floods to white, and it commits — the blade and the Color through it, both at once.

* intro
You see it first as a wrong color on the hillside above the dry
riverbed — a saturated violet the sun does not explain. As you watch,
it stands. The shape is vaguely a man's shape, taller than a man,
naked, the skin pulsing in slow waves the way a cuttlefish pulses, hues
you cannot quite settle on rolling across it from one side of the body
to the other. There are no eyes you can find. There is no expression to
find them with. In one hand it is holding a curved Tashkari blade,
gripped correctly, and that is the only thing about it that still
remembers being human. It steps down off the slope toward you. It does
not speak. Whatever walks out of the great factory does not speak.

* win
+give_gold 12
+add_tag killed_stray_vessel_1
The Color drains out of the body in a long, slow exhale, and what is
left in the dust is something that looks for a moment like a man, and
then less like one, and then not very much like anything at all. The
blade holds its shape. You leave it where it falls.

* lose
The Color washes over you in a violet that hurts to remember. The
hillside above the wash is very quiet.
